# 9. IPv6 Static Routes — Fallout Shelter

Initially, `FO-RT01` only knew about its directly connected IPv6 networks.

The Cafe networks were:

```text
2001:DB8:1:1::/64
2001:DB8:1:2::/64
```

Static routes were added:

```cisco
ipv6 route 2001:db8:1:1::/64 2001:db8:1:3::1
ipv6 route 2001:db8:1:2::/64 2001:db8:1:3::1
```

Meaning:

```text
Destination                  Next Hop
2001:DB8:1:1::/64  --------> 2001:DB8:1:3::1
2001:DB8:1:2::/64  --------> 2001:DB8:1:3::1
```

The next hop is the **Cafe router's IPv6 WAN address**.

---

# 10. IPv6 Static Routes — Cafe

The Fallout Shelter networks are:

```text
2001:DB8:1:4::/64
2001:DB8:1:5::/64
2001:DB8:1:6::/64
2001:DB8:1:7::/64
```

Routes were added on `cafe01-RT01`:

```cisco
ipv6 route 2001:db8:1:4::/64 2001:db8:1:3::2
ipv6 route 2001:db8:1:5::/64 2001:db8:1:3::2
ipv6 route 2001:db8:1:6::/64 2001:db8:1:3::2
ipv6 route 2001:db8:1:7::/64 2001:db8:1:3::2
```

The next hop is the **Fallout Shelter router's IPv6 WAN address**.

